From bea20c98d20dc68d23b81d006ad52372636b7ed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahrokh <design@cariblanco.best>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:18:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] disk tier: --conversation-cache-spill-on park (a mirror
 at the park), compaction and cancellation

The disk tier stops being only overflow. With the tier on, --conversation-cache-spill-on defaults to park: the state the request ends with (the park) is written then, by an async writer that keeps one cell per conversation holding only the newest state, so a turn with five tool calls writes once. evict is the opt-out and reproduces delta 1 byte for byte; without a spill directory both are inert.

A stored copy whose header still matches but whose common prefix with the incoming prompt is shorter than --conversation-cache-spill-divergence-tokens is a rewritten tail (a compaction or an edited history): it is discarded, not left orphaned. A request the client cancels leaves a provisional state: the live ids revert to the last --turn-token boundary, no durable copy is published of it, and the previous one is left alone.

Host tests: conversation_spill_test 102 -> 169 checks. Flags: --conversation-cache-spill-on, --conversation-cache-spill-divergence-tokens, --conversation-cache-spill-park-throttle-s.
